    <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top: 3rem;">About</p>
    <h1>Hello, I'm Damian.</h1>
    <p>
      I'm a senior software engineer in Sheffield, UK, currently building free-to-play
      iGaming products for clients like DraftKings — full solutions delivered on
      three-week cycles in a regulated industry. Alongside that, I build and run
      production AI systems: autonomous development loops on Claude Code, multi-agent
      audit pipelines for Web3 security work, and a personal-assistant harness that
      manages a real life — calendars, finances, health tracking, memory — through
      plain files and scheduled agents.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      Closed Loop is where those systems get written up properly. Each article is a
      working system explained from the inside: the architecture, the gates, and —
      most importantly — the failures. Nearly every rule in a good agentic system is
      a scar with documentation, and the articles keep the scars attached.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's a learning resource for engineers building with LLMs, and a portfolio of
      how I work: state in plain files, verification by evidence rather than
      assertion, and separation of duties enforced by capability, not prompts.
    </p>
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AI engineering</strong> — agentic loops, multi-agent orchestration, Claude Code skills/subagents, RAG pipelines, evaluation.</li>
      <li><strong>Production delivery</strong> — senior engineer at an iGaming company shipping for DraftKings and Caesars; remote contracts across iGaming and fintech.</li>
      <li><strong>Web3 security</strong> — CosmWasm/Golang audit work with a custom multi-agent auditing system; paid bounty findings.</li>
      <li><strong>Systems from scratch</strong> — I once designed and built an award-winning five-barrel microbrewery from raw materials, control electronics included. Whole-system thinking is the throughline.</li>
    </ul>
